% Rulings of U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CROSS, rulings.cbp.gov) run
% through the whole modelled tariff (tariff.le): Chapter 39 (plastics): primary forms, waste, semi-manufactures, sanitary and builders' ware, articles.
%
% One scenario per ruling, which the scenario names ("scenario ny_n345907 is,
% as stated in ruling NY N345907:"); each good is described by the facts the
% ruling states, each quoting its passage ("confer \"...\""), and the office's
% judgments — principal use, essential character, answers to claims — say who
% made them ("according to CBP"). The ruling's code is NOT a fact: it is in
% the comment "% CBP: <good> -> <code>" above each scenario; the expectation
% is the six-digit subheading the model derives, and where it differs from
% CBP's the comment says so (DISAGREES) and why.
%
% Selection (September 2026): for each six-digit subheading of Chapters 39, 61
% and 62 not covered by the first prototype, the most recent New York ruling
% (2016 or later) returned by CROSS whose codes all fall in those chapters.
% Transcribed by language-model agents following a written guide, with every
% quotation checked against the ruling's text by the verifier. See README.md.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base cbp 39 includes these resources:
    tariff.

the knowledge base cbp 39 includes:

