query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% NY N345907 (February 2025): elastomeric ethylene copolymers from Belgium.
% CBP: ELVALOY AC 3217 -> 3901.90; FUSABOND A560 -> 3901.90
scenario ny_n345907 is, as stated in ruling NY N345907:
    the kind of ELVALOY AC 3217 is pellets,
        confer "It is available in pellet form and is used in medical packaging".
    the polymer of ELVALOY AC 3217 is ethylene copolymer,
        confer "The product is a copolymer of ethylene and butyl acrylate. The ethylene monomer comprises greater than 50 percent, but less than 95 percent by weight of the copolymer".
    the kind of FUSABOND A560 is pellets,
        confer "It is available in pellet form".
    the polymer of FUSABOND A560 is ethylene copolymer,
        confer "The product is a chemically modified ethylene acrylate copolymer".
    FUSABOND A560 is chemically modified,
        confer "The product is a chemically modified ethylene acrylate copolymer".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of ELVALOY AC 3217 is 3901.90", "the subheading of FUSABOND A560 is 3901.90"].

% NY N322252 (October 2021): maleic anhydride modified propylene copolymer from Japan.
% CBP: ADMER -> 3902.30
scenario ny_n322252 is, as stated in ruling NY N322252:
    % DISAGREES: CBP gives 3902.30; the model gives 3902.90 — the ruling
    % calls the product a maleic anhydride modified propylene copolymer,
    % recorded as chemically modified, and subheading note 1(a)(3) sends a
    % chemically modified polymer to the subheading named "Other"; the form
    % is not stated (presumed a primary form).
    % the ruling names the product ADMERTM (ADMER with the trade mark sign); it
    % states no form (pellets, powder, liquid...) of the product
    the polymer of ADMER is propylene copolymer,
        confer "the product is a maleic anhydride modified propylene copolymer".
    ADMER is chemically modified,
        confer "the product is a maleic anhydride modified propylene copolymer".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of ADMER is 3902.90"].

% NY N350881 (July 2025): butadiene, methyl methacrylate, styrene copolymers from the Netherlands.
% CBP: Clearstrength E920 -> 3902.90; Clearstrength C303H -> 3902.90
scenario ny_n350881 is, as stated in ruling NY N350881:
    % a copolymer in which butadiene (an olefin) predominates: no listed
    % butadiene copolymer, so olefin polymer
    the kind of Clearstrength E920 is powder,
        confer "The product is imported in the form of white powder or pellets".
    the polymer of Clearstrength E920 is olefin polymer,
        confer "It is composed of 85 percent butadiene, 10 percent methyl methacrylate and 5 percent styrene".
    the kind of Clearstrength C303H is powder,
        confer "The product is imported in the form of white powder. It is recommended for use in high quality PVC".
    the polymer of Clearstrength C303H is olefin polymer,
        confer "It is composed of 65 percent butadiene, 8 percent methyl methacrylate and 27 percent styrene".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of Clearstrength E920 is 3902.90", "the subheading of Clearstrength C303H is 3902.90"].

% NY N284703 (April 2017): a compounded ethylene tetrafluoroethylene fluoropolymer from Korea.
% CBP: EC1378 -> 3904.69
scenario ny_n284703 is, as stated in ruling NY N284703:
    the kind of EC1378 is pellets,
        confer "is a compounded ethylene tetrafluoroethylene (ETFE) fluoropolymer, in pellet form".
    the polymer of EC1378 is fluoropolymer,
        confer "is a compounded ethylene tetrafluoroethylene (ETFE) fluoropolymer".
    EC1378 is mixed with other substances,
        confer "This product is a blend consisting of two different ETFE polymers (C-88AXMB-HT and AH-2000) mixed with carbon black".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of EC1378 is 3904.69"].

% NY N288633 (August 2017): a chlorinated polyvinyl chloride resin from Thailand.
% CBP: CPVC resin Z952 -> 3904.90
scenario ny_n288633 is, as stated in ruling NY N288633:
    % the ruling names it CPVC resin K-Value 67 (Z952); it states no form
    % (pellets, powder...) of the resin
    the polymer of CPVC resin Z952 is polyvinyl chloride,
        confer "is a chlorinated polyvinyl chloride polymer".
    CPVC resin Z952 is chemically modified,
        confer "This chemically modified product, which “is made by covalently bonding more chlorine atoms onto” the polyvinyl chloride polymer".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of CPVC resin Z952 is 3904.90"].

% NY N318445 (April 2021): poly (methyl methacrylate) polymer from Italy.
