    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of Duranol T5651 is 3907.40"].

% NY N331684 (April 2023): polyethylene terephthalate bottle flake from Thailand.
% CBP: the higher viscosity PET flake -> 3907.61; the lower viscosity PET flake -> 3907.69
scenario ny_n331684 is, as stated in ruling NY N331684:
    % the ruling distinguishes the flake by its viscosity number: 78 to 85
    % ml/g (recorded as 78, the lower bound) and 70 to less than 78 ml/g
    % (recorded as 70)
    the kind of the higher viscosity PET flake is flakes,
        confer "The product under consideration is composed of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) flakes".
    the polymer of the higher viscosity PET flake is polyethylene terephthalate,
        confer "The product under consideration is composed of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) flakes".
    the viscosity number of the higher viscosity PET flake is 78,
        confer "the PET bottle flake with a viscosity number of 78 ml/g to 85 ml/g".
    the higher viscosity PET flake is claimed to belong to waste of heading 3915,
        confer "You suggest classification in 3915.90.0010".
    the claim that the higher viscosity PET flake belongs to waste of heading 3915 is rejected,
        according to CBP, confer "Therefore the bottle PET flake cannot be classified in 3915.90.0010".
    the kind of the lower viscosity PET flake is flakes,
        confer "The product under consideration is composed of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) flakes".
    the polymer of the lower viscosity PET flake is polyethylene terephthalate,
        confer "The product under consideration is composed of polyethylene terephthalate (PET) flakes".
    the viscosity number of the lower viscosity PET flake is 70,
        confer "the PET bottle flake with a viscosity number of 70 ml/g or more but less than 78 ml/g".
    the lower viscosity PET flake is claimed to belong to waste of heading 3915,
        confer "You suggest classification in 3915.90.0010".
    the claim that the lower viscosity PET flake belongs to waste of heading 3915 is rejected,
        according to CBP, confer "Therefore the bottle PET flake cannot be classified in 3915.90.0010".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the higher viscosity PET flake is 3907.61", "the subheading of the lower viscosity PET flake is 3907.69"].

% NY N303296 (March 2019): Radpar AD-032 from Japan.
% CBP: the Radpar resin -> 3907.91
scenario ny_n303296 is, as stated in ruling NY N303296:
    % the Radpar resin is Radpar AD-032 (the name would lose its leading zero).
    % a polymer of a diallyl (di-2-propenyl) ester: an allyl, unsaturated polyester
    the kind of the Radpar resin is powder,
        confer "It will be imported in the form of white powder".
    the polymer of the Radpar resin is unsaturated polyester,
        confer "The product constists predominantly of poly (1,2-Cyclohexane dicarboxylic acid, di-2-propenyl ester)".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the Radpar resin is 3907.91"].

% NY N352351 (March 2026): a polybutylene succinate (PBS)-starch composite.
% CBP: the biopolymer-starch composite -> 3907.99
scenario ny_n352351 is, as stated in ruling NY N352351:
    the kind of the biopolymer-starch composite is pellets,
        confer "The product is pulled through a pelletizer with a rotating knife. The pellets are then loaded".
    the polymer of the biopolymer-starch composite is polyester,
        confer "It is noted to be a polybutylene succinate (PBS) - corn starch composite material".
    the biopolymer-starch composite is mixed with other substances,
        confer "It is noted to be a polybutylene succinate (PBS) - corn starch composite material".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the biopolymer-starch composite is 3907.99"].

% NY N343968 (November 2024): a two-component spray applied polyurethane foam system from Canada.
% CBP: SEALECTION 500 -> 3909.50
scenario ny_n343968 is, as stated in ruling NY N343968:
    % the ruling states no form (liquid...) of the system or its two sides
    the polymer of SEALECTION 500 is polyurethane,
        confer "is a two-component, open cell, spray applied, semirigid polyurethane foam system".
    the isocyanate side of SEALECTION 500 is a component of SEALECTION 500,
        confer "RUBINATE® M/SUPRASEC® 5005 A-Side (Polymeric MDI)".
    the polymer of the isocyanate side of SEALECTION 500 is polymeric MDI,
        confer "RUBINATE® M/SUPRASEC® 5005 A-Side (Polymeric MDI)".
    the polyol side of SEALECTION 500 is a component of SEALECTION 500,
        confer "SEALECTION® 500 B-Side (Polyether polyol blend)".
    the polymer of the polyol side of SEALECTION 500 is polyether,
        confer "SEALECTION® 500 B-Side (Polyether polyol blend)".
    SEALECTION 500 is claimed to belong to other articles of plastics of heading 3926,
        confer "You suggest that the SEALECTION® 500 should be classified in 3926.90.9989".
    the claim that SEALECTION 500 belongs to other articles of plastics of heading 3926 is rejected,
        according to CBP, confer "classification in 3926.90.9989, HTSUS, is precluded".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of SEALECTION 500 is 3909.31", "the subheading of SEALECTION 500 is 3907.29", "the subheading of SEALECTION 500 is 3909.50"]
        and unknowns ["the essential character of SEALECTION 500 is given by no single component"].

